truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.18+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Relax NVMe host NQN validation to accept NQNs without :identifier
    suffix (#44). Per NVMe-oF spec the :identifier segment is mandatory
    for subsystem NQNs but optional for host NQNs. The Linux kernel
    generates host NQNs as nqn.YYYY-MM.tld.domain with no further suffix;
    the previous regex rejected them with "Invalid NVMe host NQN", making
    NVMe-TCP completely non-functional for affected hosts. Fix makes the
    :identifier block optional in _nvme_untaint_cli_nqn; malformed NQNs
    and shell metacharacters are still rejected.

