truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.9+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix snapshot rollback when intermediate snapshots exist. PVE's qm
    rollback contract is to revert the disk to the target snapshot and
    discard anything taken after. Plugin was passing recursive=0 to TN's
    pool.snapshot.rollback, so any intermediate snapshot on the same
    dataset blocked the rollback with TN 25.10's wrapped FileExistsError:
      "Cannot rollback: more recent snapshots exist. Use recursive=True
      to destroy them. [Errno 17] Failed to rollback ... File exists"
    Two changes: volume_snapshot_rollback now passes recursive=1; the
    _tn_snapshot_rollback fallback regex also matches the TN 25.10
    wording (was matching only the old libzfs message). Verified against
    TN 25.10 snapshot_rollback_impl.py: recursive=True triggers
    _destroy_newer_snapshots on the target dataset and does not touch
    clones (recursive_clones=False) or child datasets
    (recursive_rollback=False). Matches PVE::Storage::ZFSPoolPlugin
    semantics (which calls `zfs rollback -r`).

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Tue, 23 Jun 2026 11:30:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.8+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename ZFS snapshot API calls from zfs.snapshot.* to pool.snapshot.*
    to match TrueNAS 25.10 middleware. The legacy zfs.snapshot namespace
    was removed in 25.10 and returns -32601 "Method does not exist",
    breaking qm snapshot / qm rollback / volume_snapshot_delete /
    bulk snapshot delete. Affects: pool.snapshot.query,
    pool.snapshot.create, pool.snapshot.delete, pool.snapshot.clone,
    pool.snapshot.rollback. Same fix already shipped on broker-service
    via 35281fb; this commit ports it to fix/rate-limit-connection-reuse.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Tue, 23 Jun 2026 11:00:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.7+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * truenas-plugin-broker: log every error response (lwarn). Before this
    change the daemon only logged WS lifecycle events (opened / reaping /
    startup / shutdown) and was silent when upstream RPCs failed. After
    a broker restart, the first upstream auth.login_with_api_key can be
    rejected by TN's per-IP rate limiter from prior activity, and the
    failure was invisible in the journal. Now broker logs bad request
    JSON, missing scfg fields, no-method requests, upstream RPC
    exceptions (including the dead-pool cleanup), no-response-from-
    upstream conditions, and structured JSON-RPC errors returned by TN
    (e.g. EBUSY / Rate Limit Exceeded). No behaviour change beyond logs.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Mon, 22 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.6+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add node-local session broker daemon (truenas-plugin-broker) that holds
    one authenticated WebSocket per (host, api_key) pair and proxies
    JSON-RPC for every plugin invocation via /run/truenas-plugin/broker.sock.
    Eliminates per-process re-authentication from forked qm, pvesh and
    pveproxy workers (D2). When the broker socket is absent the plugin
    falls back to the existing per-process persistent WebSocket path with
    no behavioural change.
  * Ship truenas-plugin-broker.service systemd unit, enabled and started
    by postinst before pvedaemon/pveproxy/pvestatd restart.
  * Map this branch's tn_*-prefixed scfg keys to the broker daemon's
    stable api_* wire format inside the plugin client so the broker
    binary serves both this branch and the legacy api_*-keyed branch
    without modification.
  * See wiki/D2-per-process-reauth.md for design notes.

